    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1">

                <pb facs="0009" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg1"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/577<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >2/4</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-02-01T13:00:00-05:00">February 1, 1941—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. My telegram No. 31, January 27.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1-f1"/> In conversation
                    with President<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1-f2"/> last night it was opportune for me
                    informally to mention possibility we would desire to make survey of Old
                    Providence Island and Cartagena. President readily assented but requested that
                    officers and equipment sent for this purpose be temporarily attached to Naval
                    Mission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Braden</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
